      "sourceTextSha256": "b9c57f4f9d161b947fe689bd64257ceb3a9e8a2b2a3b363c93dce16dcd0c7939",
      "text": "Day 3 · North to Imbabura: chirimoya in Guayllabamba, a family making the traditional bizcochos and layered cheese of Cayambe (coffee break included), the Miralago viewpoint over Imbabura Volcano and Lake San Pablo, and the Plaza de los Ponchos in Otavalo, one of the largest Indigenous markets in South America. Continue to Cotacachi, famous for its leather goods, and the sacred Peguche Waterfall, through a eucalyptus forest. Overnight at Hacienda Pinsaqui. (B)",
